## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to translate data-security policy into concrete export controls.

## Key Concepts
- Data minimization and redaction
- RBAC and per-session scopes
- Token-based session gating
- Centralized exporting logs and retention
- IR playbooks and containment steps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Express route sketch: enforce role-based redaction on export
app.post('/exports/statements', authorize(['viewer','exporter']), (req,res)=>{
  const fields = req.user.role==='exporter' ? fullFields : ['date','amount','balance'];
  const csv = generateCSV(data, fields);
  res.setHeader('Content-Type','text/csv');
  res.send(csv);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the export redaction in CI?
- What metrics indicate success of the control?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to apply fundamental security controls to third-party components—a common real-world risk at many companies. It evaluates your understanding of vendor vetting, data minimization, privacy controls, and incident response readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Third-party risk management
- Data minimization and PII redaction
- User consent and privacy controls
- Observability and incident response readiness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: redact PII from analytics payload
function redact(payload) {
  const redacted = { ...payload };
  if (redacted.userEmail) redacted.userEmail = "[REDACTED]";
  if (redacted.userPhone) redacted.userPhone = "[REDACTED]";
  return redacted;
}

// Example: hash identifiers before transmission
function hashIdentifier(identifier) {
  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(identifier).digest('hex');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design zero-trust controls across cloud and on‑prem, plus IR rigor.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege across IAM and Kubernetes RBAC
- OIDC-based short-lived credentials and STS
- Image provenance and SBOM
- Secret management and CI rotation
- IR containment and customer notification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: verify an OIDC-provided token expiration
function isTokenValid(token) {
  const now = Math.floor(Date.now()/1000);
  const payload = decodeJWT(token);
  return payload.exp > now;
}
```

